From: atty303 <atty303@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mfreadwrite: drain Source Reader transforms on demand

Keep a stream in an explicit draining state after the media source reaches
EOS. Send MFT_MESSAGE_COMMAND_DRAIN once per transform, but service the chain
only while a Source Reader request is pending. If downstream backpressure
outlives that request, retain the unsubmitted sample and resume it from the
next ReadSample call. Publish EOS only after the final transform is empty.

This preserves Source Reader backpressure for video and other media while
allowing split decoder output, including the final WMA frame, to be returned
over subsequent ReadSample calls instead of being discarded behind EOS. Drain
failures are returned as Source Reader errors rather than being disguised as
successful EOS.

Add an opt-in mfdrain channel that pairs drain messages, ProcessOutput calls,
and drain-related synchronous waits. State snapshots include request and
response counts so a blocked ReadSample can be attributed without enabling
per-sample or network logging.

